# SDK Coverage Testing

When adding or changing functionality in **Toggly.FeatureManagement** SDK packages, always add or update unit tests so CI coverage thresholds stay met.

## When This Applies

- New public APIs, behavior changes, or bug fixes in any SDK under this repository
- Shared utilities (`sdk-identity`, `ws-sync`, evaluation context, WebSocket refresh, caching)
- Framework adapters (React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, Astro, Remix, React Native, etc.)

## Requirements

1. **Add tests with the feature** — do not merge behavior without corresponding coverage in the same PR/commit.
2. **Run package coverage locally** before pushing (see package `package.json` scripts).
3. **Target branch coverage** — most SDK workflows fail on **branches** first; exercise both sides of conditionals (empty vs set identity/groups/claims, 304 vs 200, WS message types, `persistCache` on/off).
4. **WebSocket debounce** — refresh is debounced (~300ms); use fake timers (`jest.advanceTimersByTime`, `vi.advanceTimersByTime`, Angular `fakeAsync` + `tick`).
5. **URL assertions** — prefer `new URL(url).searchParams.get(...)` over raw encoded query strings when testing `appendEvaluationContext`.
6. **Do not lower thresholds** to make CI pass unless explicitly approved; add tests instead.

## CI Thresholds (reference)

| Package | Statements | Branches | Functions | Lines |
|---------|------------|----------|-----------|-------|
| JS core | 90% | 85% | 90% | 90% |
| Vue | 90% | 85% | 90% | 90% |
| Svelte | 90% | 84% | 90% | 90% |
| Angular lib | 90% | 80% | 90% | 90% |
| Astro | 85% | 80% | 85% | 85% |
| Remix server | 90% | 88% | 90% | 90% |

## Checklist for New SDK Behavior

- [ ] Happy path test
- [ ] Empty/null/undefined inputs where supported
- [ ] Error or fallback paths (network failure, 304, corrupt cache)
- [ ] Live-update paths if WebSocket-related
- [ ] Local `coverage` run meets thresholds for the touched package
